{\up +}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up +} BROWSE0002:0001}
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} StgMgr Navigation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 17R.5HZ}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Manager Navigation tab
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The Navigation tab gives a visual display of the position of the stage sample holder with the specimen stubs. \b N.B See \uldb Properties\plain\b\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Properties} and \uldb sample holder settings\plain\b\fs24 {\v Sample_Holder_Settings}\plain\fs24 
\par    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6485\cellx11515\pard\intbl The Navigation tab shows two views of the stage sample holder: a side-on view and a perpendicular view. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b\fs28 The side-on view
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 This view shows the selected stage sample holder and is side-on to the holder. The horizontal line shows the sample height parameter. The vertical line shows the path of the electron beam. The secondary electron detector is at the right side of sample holder. Blue grid lines show the user-set limits in the Y- and Z-direction. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b\fs28 The perpendicular view
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 This view shows a perpendicular view to the sample holder. The crossed grid lines indicate the position of the electron beam. The horizontal grid line only shows when Stage Tilt = 0\f3 \'b0\f4 . The secondary electron detector is situated on top. Blue grid lines show the user-set limits in the X- and Y-direction. 
\par\intbl A thick blue line indicates the position of the chamber door.
\par\intbl \b\fs28 Moving the stage
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 You can move the stage so that a desired part of the sample holder lies under the electron beam. \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \{bmc bm5.bmp\} Double click the left mouse button on a point of interest on the sample holder. The stage will move (XY) it under the beam.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \{bmc bm6.bmp\} Double-click the middle mouse button on a point of interest on the sample holder. The stage will move it (rotate) under the beam  
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b\fs28 Show stage scan fields\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \plain\fs24 If you have set up a stage scan pattern, you can show this pattern on the perpendicular view. Setting up a stage scan pattern can be done from the \uldb Stage Scanning\plain\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Stage_Scanning} tab\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Tick the \b Show Fields\plain\fs24  check box. A red grid will appear on the view: \{bmc bm7.bmp\} 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab \b Note\plain\fs24 : The scan field grid shows the positions of the centre of the stage, at the bottom right corner of each grid field. It does \ul not\plain\fs24  show the positions on the sample holder of the actual fields that will be visible to the user. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close Stage Manager with \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm10.shg\}\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab \b Note\plain\fs24 : if the option Sample Holder = none is selected in the \uldb Properties \plain\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Properties}page, then only a grey cross is shown\cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 
\par \page
{\up +}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up +} BROWSE0002:0002}
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} StgMgr Stage Status}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 4P6Z_J1}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Manager Status tab
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The Stage Status panel  is used to display and control the position of the motorised stage
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6465\cellx11505\pard\intbl \b\fs28 Stage Movement\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm11.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the \b Go To X\plain\fs24  or\b  Y\plain\fs24  field to open an input box to enter XY coordinates.
\par\intbl \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab Click on any other active \b Go To\plain\fs24  field to open a \b normal input value box\plain\fs24  and to enter the coordinate.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab \b Note\plain\fs24  The\b  Stage Stop \plain\fs24 button will abort stage movement. 
\par\intbl This may also be achieved by pressing F12. The \b Undo Goto\plain\fs24  button will undo the requested movement. \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \ul \b\ul\fs28 Field Movement\plain\b\fs28 {\v Field_movement_arrow_buttons}\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Use the \b Arrow buttons\plain\fs24  to move one screen up, down, left or right
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab If the \b Move using Stage Scanning fields\plain\fs24  option is checked, and a scan pattern is defined, then the Up button moves to the first field in the Scan Pattern, the Left button to the previous field, the right button to the next field. The Down button is unassigned
\par\intbl The Pause button is not assigned yet.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b\fs28 Further options\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \tab Right-Click on the other elements of the Stage Status Tab for more information
\par\intbl \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\tab Click on the tab background with the right mouse button to open the \uldb \b Status Popup Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Status_Popup_Menu}\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close \b Stage Manager\plain\fs24  with \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm13.shg\}\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f13 When the cursor changes from \{bmc bm14.bmp\}to \{bmc bm15.bmp\}help is available. Click to present the information.\f4 \cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 
\par \page
