{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} StgMgr Points List}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} CC.BB_}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Manager Points List tab
\par \pard\tx2695 \plain\fs24 This Tab displays the user-defined points on the stage. It performs the same functions as the \uldb Stage_Points_List_dialog\plain\fs24 {\v 139NVAW@Stage.hlp}. 
\par \pard\tx2695    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6465\cellx11505\pard\intbl \f13 A list of stage positions may be maintained in memory. The entries are shown in the \b Stage Points List\plain\f13\fs24 . Initially this list is empty. \f4 The data saved is the current position of the stage. If beam shift is being applied the XY stage position is modified by the Beam Offset distance to give a stage XY position with zero beam shift. Also saved are the current \b working distance\plain\fs24  and \b magnification\plain\fs24 . When moving to a stored position the beam shift is set to zero and optionally either or both of the magnification/working distance are set to the saved values\f13 .
\par\intbl \f4 
\par\intbl \f13 For additional information point to the item of interest on the picture to the right. \f6\fs20 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f13\fs24 \tab When the cursor changes from \{bmc bm14.bmp\}to \{bmc bm15.bmp\}help is available. Click to present the information.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \f4 \{bmc bm16.bmp\}Right-click on the Tab area to show the \uldb \b Points List Popup menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Points_List_Popup_Menu} \plain\f13\fs24 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \f4 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close Stage Manager with \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\f13 \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \f4 \{bmc bm17.shg\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
