\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Manager Stage Scanning tab
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Stage scan provides the facility of using the motorised stage to inspect an area of the specimen as a series of fields.
\par    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6455\cellx11485\pard\intbl \b\fs28 Setting up a scan area and scan fields\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Press the \ul Setup Wizard\plain\fs24 {\v Scan_Field_Setup_Wizard} button and go through the different steps of selecting the Scan area and creating the scan fields. 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Alternatively, select the Advance button. The \uldb Stage Scan dialog\plain\fs24 {\v 5PRL_G3@Stage.hlp} appears. 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab When the Scan pattern area is correctly set up, the fields will appear in the \ul Scan Fields\plain\fs24 {\v Scan_Fields} window
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b\fs28 Selecting a scan pattern\par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select one of the \ul Stage Scan Pattern\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_Scan_Pattern} buttons to determine in which pattern the fields are scanned.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \b\fs28 Navigation\par\pard \pard\intbl\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm19.bmp\} Go to first field
\par\intbl \{bmc bm20.bmp\} Go to previous field
\par\intbl \{bmc bm21.bmp\} Go to next field
\par\intbl \{bmc bm22.bmp\} Go to last field\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx1075 \b\fs28 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close \b Stage Manager\plain\fs24  with \{bmc bm9.bmp\}
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm23.shg\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
