{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Manager Survey tab
\par \pard \uldb \plain\b\uldb\fs24 Survey Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Overview}\plain\fs24  provides the facility to enter a defined state [\uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 ] (typically a long Working Distance and low magnification to achieve a wide field of view) in which the Specimen may be reviewed for features of interest.
\par \b\fs28    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx6475\cellx11075\pard\intbl Setting up Survey Mode
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 This dialog is used to set up conditions for \uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24  and for \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 . 
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Ensure that the \uldb \b Stage Z High and Low user limits\plain\b\fs24 {\v HE_C4L@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  are correctly set for the specimen to be reviewed, in particular the High limit to prevent collision with the Final lens. (Select the \uldb \b Stage Manager Properties tab\plain\b\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Properties}\plain\fs24  and press the \b Set\plain\fs24  \b Limits \plain\fs24 button).
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Obtain a focussed image under your normal (Survey Mode OFF) conditions.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab If required you can also define the Exit Macro.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\b Note:\plain\fs24  Survey Mode may only be used when the Stage is initialised. \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab For details of each control on the panel click on the control.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close \b Stage Manager\plain\fs24  with \{bmc bm9.bmp\}\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl \{bmc bm24.shg\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
