{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Auto Initialise Stage}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} TKXDWU}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Auto Initialise Stage}
\b\fs36\cf1 Auto Initialise Stage
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm25.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on this function to start the stage initialisation. 
\par 
\par \tab \tab \{bmc bm26.bmp\}
\par 
\par Accept with \b Yes
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 The stage will then perform it's\ul  initialisation sequence\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_initialisation_sequence}
\par 
\par Now the stage coordinates are referenced.
\par 
\par With \b No\plain\fs24  you terminate without initialising the stage.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\} \b NOTE\plain\fs24 : If the Stage is not initialised the actual Stage co-ordinates are unknown, hence the stage cannot be instructed to go to specific co-ordinates
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Backlash On}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Backlash_On}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Backlash On
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 This menu lets you switch Stage Backlash ON. or OFF.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm27.bmp\}\tab If you \ul click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} ON it is marked with \{bmc bm28.bmp\}. Backlash correction is then performed after each stage movement.
\par 
\par Backlash correction is defined in \uldb \b Preference Selection Stage\plain\b\fs24 {\v 3TQY_S@leoserv.HLP}\plain\fs24  tab.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Compucentric Mode}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Compucentric_Mode}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Backlash On;Compucentric Mode;Stage Delta}
\b\fs36\cf1 Compucentric Mode
\par \plain\fs24 This Combo box is used to select if compucentric rotation and/or Tilt is to be performed when goto tilt or rotation values are entered.
\par \b See also: \uldb \plain\uldb\fs24 Compucentric Movement\plain\fs24 {\v Compucentric_Movement}
\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Compucentric Movement}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Compucentric_Movement}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Compucentric Movement
\par \pard \plain\fs24 If a \ul Compucentric mode\plain\fs24 {\v Compucentric_Mode} is selected and a Rotate/Tilt movement is requested via the \ul Goto\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_goto} or \ul Delta\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_Delta} functions the software calculates and executes the compensating movements for the other axes to maintain the sample position in the field of view.
\par 
\par Note that calibrations are required. 
\par See \uldb Calibrate Stage Centre\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_82@dlgmgr.hlp} and  \uldb Compucentric Setup\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_83@dlgmgr.hlp}
\par 
\par See Also \uldb Stage Horizontal Alignment\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_84@dlgmgr.hlp} and \uldb Compucentric Stage Control\plain\fs24 {\v GP9BLC@stage.hlp}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Do Backlash}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Do_Backlash}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Do Backlash
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm29.bmp\}\tab \ul Clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b Do Backlash \plain\fs24 causes the stage to execute a backlash correction operation.
\par 
\par Backlash correction is defined in \uldb \b Preference Selection Stage\plain\b\fs24 {\v 3TQY_S@leoserv.HLP}\plain\fs24  tab.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Exit Survey Mode}
