\par \plain\fs24 Enter the magnification you require on switching to \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State} \plain\fs24 by requesting\b  \uldb Centre Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v N9YIPC@stage.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Note: if you change output device this value will change but will maintain the same pixel size (i.e. will not change the size of the displayed image).
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Resolution Mode State}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Resolution_Mode_State}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Do Backlash}
\b\fs36\cf1 Resolution Mode State
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Resolution Mode state is entered when \uldb \b Centre Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v N9YIPC@stage.hlp}\plain\fs24  or \uldb \b Centre Feature\plain\b\fs24 {\v T2YJNK@stage.hlp}\plain\fs24  is executed while in \uldb \b Survey Mode  State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par On entry to \b Resolution Mode State\plain\fs24  from \b Survey Mode state\plain\fs24  the current Magnification and  Working Distance replace the Survey Mode settings if the 'Save Settings' is checked on the \uldb \b Stage Manager Survey tab\plain\b\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Survey}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par On entering Resolution mode state the Magnification is set to the defined magnification (Centre Point) or to the required magnification for the Centre feature function. The working distance is set to the defined Working Distance (constrained to the Minimum achievable Working Distance and the High User Z limit ).
\par \pard 
\par The brightness is set to the value last used in Resolution Mode State.
\par 
\par If required a Fine Auto Focus is next executed followed by the Resolution  Mode Macro if defined.
\par 
\par To Exit from  Resolution Mode State press \b  <F4>\plain\fs24  
\par 
\par \b See also:\plain\fs24  \uldb \b Survey Overview\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Overview}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} resolution mode wd}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} resolution_mode_wd}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Resolution Mode Working Distance.
\par \plain\fs24 Enter the Working distance you wish to use when in \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 .
\par This is typically a short Working Distance for best resolution.
\par 
\par When going to this Working Distance the Stage Z will be increased to maintain focus.
\par It is therefore essential that the \uldb \b Stage High User Limit\plain\b\fs24 {\v HE_C4L@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  is correctly set to avoid collision with the final lens.
\par If the target Working Distance would cause the stage to contravene the High User Limit then the Working distance is correspondingly increased.
\par \pard 
\par \page
