\par \plain\fs24 The Drop Down Combo Box offers a choice of all the currently available macros.
\par 
\par Select a macro from the list and check the checkbox if you wish this macro to be executed on entering Survey Mode State (i.e. Checking the Survey Mode checkbox or returning to Survey Mode State from Resolution Mode State by pressing \b <F4>\plain\fs24 ).
\par 
\par The macro will be executed when the Auto Focus finishes, unless Auto Focus is not selected, in which case it is executed when the Stage motion is completed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey mode mag}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_mode_mag}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode Magnification
\par \plain\fs24 Enter the magnification required when in \uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 .
\par Typically this will be a low magnification .
\par 
\par Note: if you change output device this value will change but will maintain the same pixel size (i.e. will not change the size of the displayed image).
\par 
\par This magnification will only be used if the Radio Button adjacent to it is selected.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey mode remember changes}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_mode_remember_changes}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode Remember changes
\par \plain\fs24 When switching to \uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 , especially for the first time, it may be necessary to adjust focus.
\par If \b Remember changes \plain\fs24 is checked the new Working Distance as a result of focussing will replace the Target WD in the Settings.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Survey Mode State}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Survey_Mode_State}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode State
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Survey Mode state is first entered when Survey Mode is switched On (either via the \uldb \b Stage Manager Survey tab\plain\b\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Survey}\plain\fs24 ) or by switching the Survey Mode Parameter.
\par 
\par It is also entered from \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State}\plain\fs24  when\b  <F4>\plain\fs24  is pressed
\par 
\par On entry to Survey Mode State from the OFF state the current Magnification, Working Distance, Stage Z and Brightness are saved for use when Survey Mode is switched off.
\par 
\par On entering Survey mode state the Magnification is set either to the defined magnification or to the lowest achievable magnification for the conditions. The working distance is set to the defined Working Distance (constrained to the Maximum achievable Working Distance and the Low User Z limit ).
\par \pard 
\par The brightness is set to the value last used in Survey Mode State.
\par 
\par If required a Fine Auto Focus is next executed followed by the Survey Mode Macro if defined.
\par 
\par \b See also:\plain\fs24  \uldb \b Survey Overview\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Overview}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey mode status}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_mode_status}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode Status
\par \plain\fs24 This field displays the current Survey Mode status.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab OFF
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \uldb Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State}
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab \uldb Leaving Survey Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v Exit_Survey_Mode}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey mode wd}
\pard {\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_mode_wd}
\b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode Working Distance
\par \plain\fs24 Enter the Working distance you wish to use when in \uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 .
\par This is typically a long Working Distance for widest field of view.
\par 
\par When going to this Working Distance the Stage Z will be decreased to maintain focus.
\par It is therefore essential that the \uldb \b Stage Low User Limit\plain\b\fs24 {\v HE_C4L@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  is correctly set for the sample in use.
\par If the target Working Distance would cause the stage to contravene the Low User Limit then the Working distance is correspondingly decreased.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Survey Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Survey_Overview}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Overview
\par \pard \plain\b\fs24 Survey Mode\plain\fs24  provides the facility to enter a defined state [\uldb \b Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 ] (typically a long Working Distance and low magnification to achieve a wide field of view) in which the Specimen may be reviewed for features of interest.
\par 
\par While in \b Survey Mode State\plain\fs24  if a \uldb \b Centre Point\plain\b\fs24 {\v N9YIPC@stage.hlp}\plain\fs24  function is executed the software, in addition to moving the selected point to centre screen, switches to another defined state [\uldb \b Resolution Mode state\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode_State}\plain\fs24 ] (typically a short working distance and higher magnification for better resolution) for examination of the point of interest.
\par \pard 
\par Similarly if a \uldb \b Centre Feature\plain\b\fs24 {\v T2YJNK@stage.hlp}\plain\fs24  function is executed while in \b Survey Mode State\plain\fs24  the software, in addition to moving the area selected to the centre of the screen and increasing magnification to fill the image, switches to \b Resolution Mode state\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par If in \b Resolution State\plain\fs24  the Key \b <F4> \plain\fs24 will return to \b Survey Mode state\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Switching off \b Survey Mode\plain\fs24  returns to the conditions which existed when \b Survey Mode\plain\fs24  was switched On.
\par \pard 
\par To set up conditions for Survey Mode State and Resolution Mode State display the \uldb \b Stage Manager Survey tab\plain\b\fs24 {\v StgMgr_Survey}\plain\fs24  from the Interface Main Menu \b Stage - Survey Mode - Settings \plain\fs24 or directly from the \b Stage Manager Control panel
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey settings load}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_settings_load}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Load Survey Settings
\par \plain\fs24 This button allows the user to select a survey Settings file (*.SRV) for loading.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} survey settings save}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} survey_settings_save}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Save Survey Settings
\par \plain\fs24 This button allows the user to save the current survey settings to a file (*.SRV) in the user Directory.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Track Z}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Track_Z}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Track Z
\par \plain\fs24 If this option is selected then when the Stage Z is moved the Working Distance is changed to attempt to keep the image in focus.
\par This is not precise but will keep the working distance close to the required setting.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Undo Stage Goto}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Undo_Stage_Goto}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Undo Stage Goto
\par \plain\fs24 When a \b stage goto\plain\fs24  is requested the stage position is saved before execution.
\par Pressing the \b Undo Stage Goto\plain\fs24  button will move the stage back to the saved position.
\par The function is only enabled when a stored value is available.
\par Note that Stage movements other than \b Go To \plain\fs24 are not included in this function (e.g. movements via the joystick)
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Z move on Vent}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Z_move_on_Vent}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Z move on Vent
\par \plain\fs24 If this option is selected  Z is moved down when the chamber is ventilated to clear the stage from the pole piece.
\par 
\par This may only be modified with \uldb Supervisor privilege\plain\fs24 {\v XTAC5O@admin32.hlp}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Sample Holder Settings}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 14IHIM4}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Sample Holder Settings
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Brings up the settings edit box:
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5145\cellx9015\pard\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Set the Spacer Thickness (in mm). The optional spacer block is manually fitted under the stage ZTR Module to reduce the height between the sample and the final lens. 
\par\intbl \b Note:\plain\fs24  The spacer thickness is \b\ul not \plain\fs24 auto - detectable by software!
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Set the Sample Holder rotational Offset (in degrees). The sample holder connects to the ZTR Module via a dovetail mounting. Depending on machine/stage type the sample holder is rotated. This correction offset allows the sample holder graphic to be more accurately displayed.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Set the Specimen Height (in mm). This displays a dotted line above the top of the specimen holder(s). This value represents the distance between the surface of the sample holder and the top of the specimen.
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm42.bmp\}\par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl Use the sliders to change values. You can also double-click to enter values manually.\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage XY+Z}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_XY_Z}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Limits;Move XY Only;Protected Z}
\b\fs36\cf1 Stage XY+Z
\par \plain\fs24 
\par If this checkbox is checked the Z axis is moved when the stage is moved in the direction of the tilt axis.
\par The amount of the Z Movement is determined by the \uldb \b Tilt Correction\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8AC6K1@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24  angle.
\par \page
